http://www.fbi.gov/ucr/ucr.htm  FRI Uniform Crime Reports
.  Includes "Crime in the United States"  (Crime in the United States (CIUS) is an annual publication in which the FBI compiles volume and rate of crime offenses for the nation, the states, and individual agencies. This report also includes arrest, clearance, and law enforcement employee data.) for 2003 back to 1995, which looks potentially useful.  Where can I find data further back than '95?

Now, when did the various states reform their CCW?

John Lott's done _the_ major research on this.  His raw data is available on his web site http://www.johnlott.org/ (but note "When downloading the data from here you promise not to give this data to others. If they want to obtain the data, they may simply come to this web site and download it for themselves.")

And, of course, the good people at ATF:  http://www.atf.gov/ , though they don't look like they have much in the way of crime stats.


Gun Facts (pdf) http://www.keepandbeararms.com/downloads/GunFacts_v3.2.pdf .  See pages 38-40 for CCW related propaganda.

